name: sim.readTexture
description: Retrieves the RGB data (or a portion of it) related to a specific texture
luaSynopsis: bytes textureData = sim.readTexture(int textureId, int options, int posX = 0, int posY = 0, int sizeX = 0, int sizeY = 0)
pythonSynopsis: buffer textureData = sim.readTexture(int textureId, int options, int posX = 0, int posY = 0, int sizeX = 0, int sizeY = 0)
inputs:
1. textureId: ID of the texture. See also simGetTextureId.
2. options: reserved for future functionality. Set to zero.
3. posX / posY: x/y position of the texture portion to retrieve. Set to [0 0] to retrieve the full texture
4. sizeX / sizeY: x/y size of the texture portion to retrieve. Set to [0 0] to retrieve the full texture
outputs:
1. textureData: texture data
